    "q-332587": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332587",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"30px\" align=\"center\">${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td width=\"40px\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-5}}</td>\n<td width=\"30px\" align=\"center\">{{field-6}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-7}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-8}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=1\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+(-4)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+2\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+2\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+4\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
