    "q-333007": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333007",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2}$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} \\\\ -2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} \\\\ -2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t+1 \\\\ 8t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0t+{a}_{1} \\\\ 0t+{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}({a}_{2}-2)t+({b}_{2}+1) \\\\ (-2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+8)t+(-2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2})\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2}-2=0 \\\\ -2{a}_{1}-3{a}_{2}+8=0 \\\\ {b}_{2}+1={a}_{1} \\\\ -2{b}_{1}-3{b}_{2}={a}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first two equations, we get \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2,\\,{a}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting these into the third and fourth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=0,\\,{b}_{1}=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
