    "q-333611": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333611",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}-2t+2 \\\\ -3{t}^{2}+5t-1\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(0)} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3(0)}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-(0)^{2}+2 \\\\ (0)^{2}-0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2 \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2=8 \\\\ {c}_{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=6.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-7.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-7\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
