    "q-333636": {
      "dom_id": "step-q333636",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the missing coefficients in the solution to the initial value problem, shown above.\n\n$x(t)=$ \n{{field-1}} \n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "We are told that the general solution to the system is \n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0} \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0){e}^{-0}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+3=7 \\\\ -{c}_{2}+2=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=4.$ From the second equation, we have ${c}_{2}=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]-5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t){e}^{-t} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
